s are still being decided.","note":"Recent growth swings across a very wide range, so this reading may be tracking a price or demand cycle rather than the industry's age. Treat the stage with caution. Classified from market-cap-weighted industry aggregates. These in-house averages include only companies that survived to today, which flatters the history a little."},"scorecard":{"valueScore":74.45,"rank":1,"peers":12,"integrity":[{"id":"goodwill_base_effect","question":"Is a large write-down in an earlier year making Technology's recent profit growth look stronger than the underlying business actually improved?","tier":"One-time gains and outliers","severity":"high","value":0.9463274065828504,"threshold":0.15,"detail":"Aggregate goodwill fell 95% into 2024, then profit growth came in at 82% in 2025. Growth off a written-down base overstates the recovery."},{"id":"ebit_cv","question":"Are Technology's earnings swinging so much from year to year that a single year says little about the real earning power, so that a multi-year average is the fairer read?","tier":"One-time gains and outliers","severity":"high","value":0.8491762150834846,"threshold":0.25,"detail":"Year-over-year operating income swings with a spread of 85% around its average (flag at 25%). In a group this cyclical, one strong year says little; judge it on multi-year medians."},{"id":"deferred_rev_drawdown","question":"Is Technology pulling sales forward from future periods, drawing down deferred revenue while still reporting growth in the current year?","tier":"One-time gains and outliers","severity":"high","value":0.5853261644566566,"threshold":0.15,"detail":"Deferred revenue fell 59% while reported revenue grew 31%. That reads as demand pulled forward from next year."},{"id":"roe_roic_sign","question":"Do Technology's return on equity and return on invested capital point in the same direction, or do the two disagree in a way that suggests the equity figure is distorted by buybacks or negative book value?","tier":"How the average is built","severity":"high","value":0.3228061711338088,"threshold":null,"detail":"ROE says 32% while ROIC says -10%. When the two disagree this hard, the equity denominator is broken (usually negative book equity from buybacks). Trust ROIC."},{"id":"gm_swing","question":"Did Technology's gross margin move too far in a single year to be a genuine change in the business, rather than a shift in product mix or an accounting change?","tier":"One-time gains and outliers","severity":"medium","value":0.06586797027865954,"threshold":0.05,"detail":"Gross margin moved 7% in one year (55% to 48%). Cost structures rarely move that fast; mix shifts and accounting changes do."},{"id":"base_year_growth","question":"Is Technology's headline growth rate this year mostly a rebound off a depressed or loss-making prior year, rather than real new progress?","tier":"One-time gains and outliers","severity":"medium","value":0.8229765221185307,"threshold":0.5,"detail":"Profit growth of 82% in 2025 comes off a depressed 2024 base. Treat the percentage as not meaningful; look at the level against 3-year history instead."},{"id":"receivables_vs_revenue","question":"Are Technology's receivables growing faster than its sales, which can mean revenue is being booked ahead of the cash actually arriving?","tier":"One-time gains and outliers","severity":"medium","value":0.11528020250300458,"threshold":0.1,"detail":"Receivables grew 12% faster than revenue in 2025. Sales booked ahead of cash is the classic end-of-cycle tell."}]}}